# Project Rules

## Stack
- Language/framework: <e.g. TypeScript, Node 20, Next.js>
- Package manager: <npm/pnpm/yarn>
- Testing: <e.g. Vitest, Jest>

## Conventions
- Commit messages follow Conventional Commits (feat, fix, docs, chore, refactor, test)
- Code formatted with <prettier/eslint — name your setup>
- Branch naming: feature/*, fix/*

## Commands
- Install deps: `npm install`
- Run dev server: `npm run dev`
- Run tests: `npm test`
## Lessons from FE-04 (vague vs. precise prompting drill)

- Forms use react-hook-form + zod for state and validation; never uncontrolled inputs with manual state.
- Conditionally required fields (e.g. a field only required when a toggle is on) must be enforced in the zod schema via `superRefine`, not just in the UI.
- After generating any new component, verify it is actually imported and rendered from `App.tsx` (or an equivalent entry point) and that `npm run dev` serves it without errors in the browser — passing unit tests alone do not confirm the app runs.